cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use WRRA-M 0.4, please cite this research note."
title: "WRRA-M 0.4: Common-Carrier Metric Origin of Filter Compatibility"
type: article
authors:
  - family-names: Choi
    given-names: Wonsik
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0001-4263-9772"
    email: "janefather@gmail.com"
version: "0.4"
date-released: 2026-10-01
license: CC-BY-4.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/Wonsik-Choi-janefather/wrra-m-0.1"
url: "https://github.com/Wonsik-Choi-janefather/wrra-m-0.1"
abstract: >-
  WRRA-M 0.4 tests whether the fifteen-channel common carrier of Minimal
  Computation Cosmology can supply the compatibility structure required by
  the sixteen-channel filter problem. It gives a conditional extension by one
  transported gauge-neutral channel, distinguishes gauge-current neutrality
  from transport absence, and defines compatibility as negative squared
  mismatch in a positive common-carrier response metric. The two free 0.3
  selection gaps then reduce exactly to carrier-metric alignment products. An
  exact finite witness proves that the positive-gap region is nonempty, while
  numerical microscopic response signatures remain open.
keywords:
  - WRRA
  - Wonsik Reality Renderer Architecture
  - meta-dimensional
  - common carrier
  - fifteen-to-sixteen-channel extension
  - null-lift criterion
  - response metric
  - filter compatibility
  - selection gap
  - right-handed neutrino
